    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d300">

                <pb facs="0449" n="361" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg361"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Batcheller.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-06-16"><hi rendition="#italic">June 16,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 71.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have had the pleasure to receive your No.
                    79 of the 27th ultimo, reporting the delivery into your possession of the
                    cannon, known as “Long Tom,” formerly a part of the armament of the brig <hi
                        rendition="#italic">General Armstrong.</hi></p>
                <p>Your dispatch has been read with interest, and a copy inclosed to the Secretary
                    of the Navy, in connection with his letter of March 28, 1892, and to Mr. Samuel
                    C. Reid, of this city.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
